From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qatcod <79017227+qatcod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 02:53:01 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] 09560: [x86] Zero-extend 32-bit register destinations in
 64-bit mode

#9325 Zero-extend the XCHG memory form's register destination

GP-7027 covered the rest of the instructions from this issue, but
XCHG m32,Reg32 in lockable.sinc still writes its 32-bit register
destination without clearing the upper half of the 64-bit alias. Its own
register forms, XCHG EAX,Rmr32 and XCHG Rmr32,Reg32, already build the
check, as does the neighbouring XADD memory form after GP-7027.
---
 Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc
index 71fb594353..556cfe3712 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc
@@ -1236,7 +1236,7 @@ define pcodeop InterlockedExchangeAdd64;
     Reg16 = InterlockedExchange16(Mem, Reg16);
 }
 
-:XCHG^xacq_xrel_prefx^alwaysLock Mem,Reg32	is vexMode=0 & xacq_xrel_prefx & alwaysLock & opsize=1 & byte=0x87; (check_Reg32_dest & Reg32) ... & Mem
+:XCHG^xacq_xrel_prefx^alwaysLock Mem,Reg32	is vexMode=0 & xacq_xrel_prefx & alwaysLock & opsize=1 & byte=0x87; Mem & (check_Reg32_dest & Reg32) ...
 {
     Reg32 = InterlockedExchange(Mem, Reg32);
     build check_Reg32_dest;
-- 
